<programme start="20261121170000 +0000" stop="20261121203000 +0000" channel="FS1 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Northwestern at Minnesota</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Minnesota Golden Gophers (5-5) host the Northwestern Wildcats (6-4) at Huntington Bank Stadium in a Big Ten game. Both sides aim to break a three-game skid. Northwestern lost against Ohio State 28-19, while Minnesota fell to Penn State 42-14.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261121203000 +0000" stop="20261122000000 +0000" channel="FS1 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Rutgers at Penn State</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Big Ten action continues as Rutgers (2-8, 1-6) takes on Penn State (6-4, 3-4) at Beaver Stadium. Rutgers seeks to end a four-game skid after a 31-0 shutout loss to Nebraska, while Penn State seeks to make it four straight wins behind Rocco Becht.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261122000000 +0000" stop="20261122033000 +0000" channel="FS1 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Arizona at Kansas State</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Kansas State Wildcats (4-6) host the No. 19 Arizona Wildcats (7-3) at Bill Snyder Family Stadium in a Big 12 Conference game. Kansas State aims to break a four-game losing streak, while Arizona has an alternate win-loss record in their last four.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261122033000 +0000" stop="20261122070000 +0000" channel="FS1 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Hawaii at Nevada</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Nevada Wolf Pack (4-6, 3-3 Mountain West) face the Hawaii Rainbow Warriors (3-7, 2-5). Nevada enters after snapping a two-game skid by beating Northern Illinois 28-7. Hawaii fell 21-13 to North Dakota State and relies on Micah Alejado.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261122070000 +0000" stop="20261122100000 +0000" channel="FS1 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Ohio State at Nebraska</sub-title><desc lang="en">The No. 14 Buckeyes (7-3, 5-2 Big Ten) face the Cornhuskers (6-4, 3-4) at Memorial Stadium. Ohio State enters after a 28-19 victory against Northwestern behind Luke Fahey, while Nebraska snapped a skid and beat Rutgers for a shutout 31-0 win.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261122100000 +0000" stop="20261122120000 +0000" channel="FS1 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Basketball</title><sub-title lang="en">Michigan at Villanova</sub-title><desc lang="en">The No. 18 Michigan Wolverines face the Villanova Wildcats in an NCAA Division I Men&apos;s game. Michigan rides a two-game win streak with Trey McKenney, while Villanova lost 81-61 to Pittsburgh on Nov. 17 with Devin Royal in non-conference play.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Basketball</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191260_b_v8_az.jpg"/></programme>
